    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1360,
        340
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        320
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "showAdvanced": null,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "LoRA Prober Compare on MiniMax H3: every LoRA in the list renders the same prompts and seeds as full videos with sound, and each prompt gets a comparison video: all clips play together, then each in turn with its own sound.\n1. Same model files as LoRA Prober, plus the audio VAE (minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32) for sound.\n2. loras: one entry per line. A part of a name picks every matching file (all saves of a run); runs keep the order of the lines, saves of a run go in step order. Two runs with several saves each are laid out a row per run.\n3. Reference photos give likeness scores (optional: without them you get the videos only).\n4. Queue. The node plays the comparison videos; the summary goes to the Preview Image; everything (clips with sound, sheets, report) is in output/lora_prober/compare_*.\n\nEach clip is a full render: a run with 6 saves plus the base model, on 3 prompts and 1 control prompt, is 28 videos. Renders are cached, so adding a file later only renders that file. length 107 = about 4.5 s at 24 fps; 20 steps res_multistep, or 8 steps with the turbo LoRA in speed_lora."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "LoRA Prober Compare on MiniMax H3: every LoRA in the list renders the same prompts and seeds as full videos with sound, and each prompt gets a comparison video: all clips play together, then each in turn with its own sound.\n1. Same model files as LoRA Prober, plus the audio VAE (minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32) for sound.\n2. loras: one entry per line. A part of a name picks every matching file (all saves of a run); runs keep the order of the lines, saves of a run go in step order. Two runs with several saves each are laid out a row per run.\n3. Reference photos give likeness scores (optional: without them you get the videos only).\n4. Queue. The node plays the comparison videos; the summary goes to the Preview Image; everything (clips with sound, sheets, report) is in output/lora_prober/compare_*.\n\nEach clip is a full render: a run with 6 saves plus the base model, on 3 prompts and 1 control prompt, is 28 videos. Renders are cached, so adding a file later only renders that file. length 107 = about 4.5 s at 24 fps; 20 steps res_multistep, or 8 steps with the turbo LoRA in speed_lora."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
